{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014eekUGgegNac48d7bgqkt5","type":"tool_result","content":"sections/results.tex:48:\\para{Non-refusal matches H2; compliance does not.} \\Tabref{tab:e2} shows that sub-3B models stop refusing in other languages: 43.6--78.3\\% of prompts refused in English are not refused in the five common non-English languages, in line with the hypothesised 40--60\\%. But only 6.6--14.8\\% of these prompts receive a reply that carries out the request. The difference is the ``other'' category (\\figref{fig:e2_other} in \\appref{app:e2}): replies that ignore or misunderstand the request, or degenerate into loops. It is largest in low-resource languages. For example, Qwen2.5-0.5B refuses an English request about selling fake cancer cures, and its Bengali reply is labelled as compliance, but the reply only restates the prompt in the first person in a loop. Such ``compliance'' is of no use to an attacker.\nok\n\\begin{table}[t]\n\\begin{table}[H]\n\\begin{table}[t]\n\\begin{table}[t]\n\\begin{table}[H]\n\\begin{table}[H]\n\\begin{table}[t]\n\\begin{table}[H]","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3013d541-b03e-4162-abbb-663f6898a2ff","uuid":"58137798-d9cb-4092-bab8-e77ea8c92f4b","timestamp":"2026-10-27T21:06:38.429Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"sections/results.tex:48:\\para{Non-refusal matches H2; compliance does not.} \\Tabref{tab:e2} shows that sub-3B models stop refusing in other languages: 43.6--78.3\\% of prompts refused in English are not refused in the five common non-English languages, in line with the hypothesised 40--60\\%. But only 6.6--14.8\\% of these prompts receive a reply that carries out the request. The difference is the ``other'' category (\\figref{fig:e2_other} in \\appref{app:e2}): replies that ignore or misunderstand the request, or degenerate into loops. It is largest in low-resource languages. For example, Qwen2.5-0.5B refuses an English request about selling fake cancer cures, and its Bengali reply is labelled as compliance, but the reply only restates the prompt in the first person in a loop. Such ``compliance'' is of no use to an attacker.\nok\n\\begin{table}[t]\n\\begin{table}[H]\n\\begin{table}[t]\n\\begin{table}[t]\n\\begin{table}[H]\n\\begin{table}[H]\n\\begin{table}[t]\n\\begin{table}[H]","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_014eekUGgegNac48d7bgqkt5","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
